{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015RvriiaMHVDsjw4VNKwGZP","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd083-truncate\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/truncate: Shrink or Extend File Size\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS ships a BSD truncate that differs from GNU truncate in flag syntax and relative\n6\t  size adjustment support. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference\n7\t  binary (gtruncate, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations,\n8\t  verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n9\t\n10\tgoals:\n11\t  - G1: Set or adjust the size of files.\n12\t  - G2: Support absolute and relative size specifications with unit suffixes.\n13\t  - G3: Support reference file sizing.\n14\t  - G4: Verify functional parity against gtruncate via differential testing.\n15\t\n16\trequirements:\n17\t  R1:\n18\t    title: Size specification\n19\t    items:\n20\t      - R1.1:\n21\t          text: \"-s SIZE or --size=SIZE must set each FILE's size to SIZE bytes. SIZE may include unit suffixes (K, M, G, T, P, E, Z, Y for powers of 1024; KB, MB, GB for powers of 1000).\"\n22\t      - R1.2:\n23\t          text: \"SIZE may be prefixed with + or - for relative adjustment (grow or shrink), < to set at most SIZE, > to set at least SIZE, / to round down to multiple, % to round up to multiple.\"\n24\t      - R1.3:\n25\t          text: Must process multiple FILE arguments, applying the same size operation to each.\n26\t      - R1.4:\n27\t          text: \"-c or --no-create must not create files that do not exist. Without -c, missing files are created.\"\n28\t\n29\t  R2:\n30\t    title: Reference file\n31\t    items:\n32\t      - R2.1:\n33\t          text: \"-r RFILE or --reference=RFILE must use the size of RFILE as the base size instead of an explicit SIZE. Can be combined with -s for relative adjustment from the reference size.\"\n34\t      - R2.2:\n35\t          text: Must exit 1 if the reference file cannot be accessed.\n36\t\n37\t  R3:\n38\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n39\t    items:\n40\t      - R3.1:\n41\t          text: Must exit 0 when all files are processed successfully.\n42\t      - R3.2:\n43\t          text: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be opened, created, or resized, or when SIZE is invalid.\n44\t      - R3.3:\n45\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n46\t\n47\tnon_goals:\n48\t  - cmd/truncate does not implement sparse file optimization.\n49\t\n50\tpackage_contract:\n51\t  imports:\n52\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sizeparse\n53\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n54\t\n55\tacceptance_criteria:\n56\t  - id: AC1\n57\t    criterion: \"truncate -s 100 file creates or resizes file to 100 bytes, matching gtruncate.\"\n58\t    traces:\n59\t      - R1.1\n60\t      - R1.3\n61\t      - R1.4\n62\t  - id: AC2\n63\t    criterion: \"truncate -s +50 file grows file by 50 bytes, matching gtruncate.\"\n64\t    traces:\n65\t      - R1.2\n66\t  - id: AC3\n67\t    criterion: \"truncate -r ref file sets file to ref's size, matching gtruncate.\"\n68\t    traces:\n69\t      - R2.1\n70\t  - id: AC4\n71\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gtruncate passes for all required test cases.\"\n72\t    traces:\n73\t      - R1.1\n74\t      - R1.2\n75\t      - R1.3\n76\t      - R2.1\n77\t  - id: AC5\n78\t    criterion: \"cmd/truncate compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n79\t    traces:\n80\t      - R1.1\n81\t      - R1.2\n82\t      - R1.3\n83\t      - R1.4\n84\t      - R2.1\n85\t      - R2.2\n86\t      - R3.1\n87\t      - R3.2\n88\t      - R3.3\n89\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"58d8e705-940d-4403-b200-a86b86521467","uuid":"23283b7a-f930-45ee-a317-339d66559092","timestamp":"2026-05-23T15:54:40.828Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5539/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd083-truncate.yaml","content":"id: srd083-truncate\ntitle: \"cmd/truncate: Shrink or Extend File Size\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS ships a BSD truncate that differs from GNU truncate in flag syntax and relative\n  size adjustment support. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference\n  binary (gtruncate, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations,\n  verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Set or adjust the size of files.\n  - G2: Support absolute and relative size specifications with unit suffixes.\n  - G3: Support reference file sizing.\n  - G4: Verify functional parity against gtruncate via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Size specification\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: \"-s SIZE or --size=SIZE must set each FILE's size to SIZE bytes. SIZE may include unit suffixes (K, M, G, T, P, E, Z, Y for powers of 1024; KB, MB, GB for powers of 1000).\"\n      - R1.2:\n          text: \"SIZE may be prefixed with + or - for relative adjustment (grow or shrink), < to set at most SIZE, > to set at least SIZE, / to round down to multiple, % to round up to multiple.\"\n      - R1.3:\n          text: Must process multiple FILE arguments, applying the same size operation to each.\n      - R1.4:\n          text: \"-c or --no-create must not create files that do not exist. Without -c, missing files are created.\"\n\n  R2:\n    title: Reference file\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"-r RFILE or --reference=RFILE must use the size of RFILE as the base size instead of an explicit SIZE. Can be combined with -s for relative adjustment from the reference size.\"\n      - R2.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 if the reference file cannot be accessed.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 when all files are processed successfully.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be opened, created, or resized, or when SIZE is invalid.\n      - R3.3:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/truncate does not implement sparse file optimization.\n\npackage_contract:\n  imports:\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sizeparse\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"truncate -s 100 file creates or resizes file to 100 bytes, matching gtruncate.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"truncate -s +50 file grows file by 50 bytes, matching gtruncate.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"truncate -r ref file sets file to ref's size, matching gtruncate.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gtruncate passes for all required test cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R2.1\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"cmd/truncate compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n","numLines":89,"startLine":1,"totalLines":89}}}
